  "ModelfileGuide.Hide": "Hide guide",
  "ModelfileGuide.Intro": "Modelfile is Ollama's configuration file for creating custom models. Use FROM / SYSTEM / TEMPLATE / PARAMETER directives to define the model's source, behavior, chat template, and sampling parameters.",
  "ModelfileGuide.Show": "Show guide",
  "ModelfileGuide.Step1Body": "Enter a base model name (e.g. qwen2.5:7b, llama3.2:3b) in the Quick Generator's Base Model field. The base must be pulled first.",
  "ModelfileGuide.Step1Title": "① Set FROM",
  "ModelfileGuide.Step2Body": "System Prompt sets the model's role & style (e.g. 'You are a senior Python engineer'). Template customizes chat format. The + buttons on the right add temperature (randomness 0-1), top_p, top_k, etc. to the PARAMETER block.",
  "ModelfileGuide.Step2Title": "② Tune SYSTEM / parameters",
  "ModelfileGuide.Step3Body": "Click 'Generate' to write parameters into the editor. 'Validate' checks syntax. Enter a Name (e.g. my-qwen) and click 'Create Model'. Use the new name for inference.",
  "ModelfileGuide.Step3Title": "③ Generate → Validate → Create",
  "ModelfileGuide.Step4Body": "'Save' writes Modelfile content to .txt/.modelfile for sharing/version control. 'Open' loads an existing file. Both work without Ollama running.",
  "ModelfileGuide.Step4Title": "④ Save / Load (optional)",
