  "Settings.UseNvidiaGpu": "Use NVIDIA GPU Monitoring",
  "SettingsGuide.BodyBehavior": "'Minimize to tray on close' controls the × button. 'Start minimized' for auto-start. 'Start with Windows' adds a Run registry entry. 'Confirm dangerous ops' prompts before delete/stop. 'Allow delete/release' disables safeguards. 'Telemetry' is off by default. 'NVIDIA GPU monitoring' needs nvidia-smi.",
  "SettingsGuide.BodyCustom": "'Custom Ollama Executable' is for a non-standard ollama.exe path (e.g. portable install). 'Custom Models Directory' stores models elsewhere. Both default to standard locations when empty. Verify discovery on the Diagnostics page.",
  "SettingsGuide.BodyGeneral": "Default 127.0.0.1:11434 matches a standard Ollama install. Change only if Ollama listens on a non-default address (WSL, remote server, custom proxy). Restart Ollama after change, or verify via the Diagnostics page.",
  "SettingsGuide.BodyLogging": "'Log level': more detail = more records but bigger files. 'Max log size' auto-rotates when reached. 'Max log files' deletes oldest beyond limit. Logs are in the data directory's logs subfolder.",
  "SettingsGuide.BodyRefresh": "How often each page polls the Ollama API (seconds). Ollama interval = health check; Running/GPU/Models = running models / GPU info / model list. Shorter = more real-time, but more CPU/network. 5-10 seconds is recommended.",
  "SettingsGuide.BodyStartup": "Override Ollama env vars at start (e.g. OLLAMA_NUM_GPU=99, OLLAMA_HOST=0.0.0:0). One KEY=VALUE per line. Leave empty if unsure.",
  "SettingsGuide.Hide": "Hide settings guide",
  "SettingsGuide.Intro": "All Custom fields are optional. Leaving them empty uses Ollama defaults / PATH auto-detection. Default values work for most users. Click 'Save and Apply' at the bottom after changes.",
